## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate chaos into a concrete, beginner-friendly incident playbook that uses service mesh metrics, cache behavior, and safe rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Service mesh observability and circuit-breakers
- Cache degradation and degraded routing
- Safe blast radius and rollback timing
- Synthetic validation of end-to-end latency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo synthetic check (for validation)
async function runSyntheticCheck() {
  const t0 = Date.now();
  await httpGet('/health');
  const dt = Date.now() - t0;
  return dt; // ms latency
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you simulate network partition in a controlled test?
- What changes if Istio vs Linkerd is used for the mesh?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests planning of safe, multi-region rollout with feature flags and clear rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Progressive rollout
- Feature flags
- Telemetry and SLO-aligned signals
- Cache invalidation/versioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for rollout gating
const enabled = getFlag("new_api_behavior");
if (enabled && regions.includes(currentRegion)) {
  useNewBehavior();
} else {
  useOldBehavior();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this if some regions have mandatory latency budgets?
- How would you integrate with an incident response playbook?
